…} × initial `bw.bits` ∈ {0,63,64,100,`0xFFFFFFFF`,…})\n- 3,000,000 xorshift fuzz cases\n\nResult — **3,031,200 cases, 0 mismatches** against the default cmake build, and also 0 mismatches against C rebuilt at `-O1`, `-O2`, `-O3`, and `-Os`.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn bitwriter_add(...) -> c_int`\n- `cargo build --release` succeeds with no warnings; `target/release/libtranslated_rust.so` produced.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I named the crate `translated_rust` (after this directory). The C build derives its library name from the parent directory of `c_src`, so if your harness loads the Rust `.so` by a specific hard-coded filename other than `libtranslated_rust.so`, tell me the expected name and I'll rename the `[lib] name`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":35101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1005,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d64e826-494e-42fa-bc48-c790193e7104","uuid":"a68acbc6-19fb-4413-af24-94ab86dae0ff","timestamp":"2026-08-18T15:04:35.363Z"}
